think With fe25519 GREEN and sent (sixth rung, HEAD 348c9e04f7 / amend d25c8e5570), the direct next crux toward Ed25519 is the group law — point add and double over the proven field. Non-gated: a curve point is arithmetic, not a key or a signature.
think Crux-first scoping: the full Ed25519 wants scalar multiplication and point decode too, but the tractable keystone is add + double + neg + sub + compression, composed purely over fe25519's public API. Point decode (sqrt-based) and the scalar ladder become their own later rounds.
think Avoided needing my own point decode this round by loading test points from Zig's Edwards25519 coordinates through each coordinate's canonical byte form (from_zig), so parity compares two independent group laws on the same projective representative. Compression (the only inversion) I do build, since it is just fe.invert + fe.mul + a sign bit.
think Derived the curve constant 2d in our own field arithmetic — d = mul(neg(121665), invert(121666)), then d+d — so no borrowed Zig/Monocypher limb literal enters the tree. Clean-room honest.
think Wrote crypto/ed25519_group.rye: Point{x,y,z,t}, fe_zero/fe_one/fe_neg/fe_sq2 helpers, edwards_d2, dbl and add (RFC 8032 §5.1.4 extended-coordinate formulas), neg, sub, to_bytes (compression). Every fn asserts positive contracts.
obs GREEN on the first metal pass — no build fix needed. The Zig-Edwards25519 parity net would flag any wrong formula term across dbl/add/sub/neg and did not.
obs Algebraic known-answers all held: base point compresses to its published encoding, identity to Y=1, B+B=2B, and B+(-B)=identity — group-theoretic checks independent of the byte-parity net.
obs tame_style_check bans clean; the new file lands in none of the ratchet lists. Composes entirely over fe25519 — no new field math, no new std.crypto call.
obs Honest scope held: no key, no signing, no network, no funds, no real device — no custody gate crossed. Ed25519's signing with an identity key stays its own gated round; even the scalar-multiplication ladder is a later non-gated round. Monocypher-source parity stays the held-fetch horizon; constant-time timing-safety a separate named horizon.
